{
  "provider": "prismhr",
  "entity": "benefit_enrollment",
  "notes": [
    "One BenefitEnrollment per getBenefitPlans benefitPlan[] item (D-049), id from (client, employee, planId). Every planDetail[] row is kept in plan_details (11 of 53 sampled plans have several, up to 6). Premium amounts carry no stated period, so plan_details[].amount_period is null with not_provided. The enrollment's own coverage_level is null with not_provided: only detail rows carry planType.",
    "getEmployeePremium is called per (employee, plan); its rates are kept raw in that enrollment's provider_extensions. Settled offline (D-084): getDeductions amount is the per-pay deduction (LTD 9.38 equals the voucher empContrib); billingRates.employeeAmount is documented only as the employee billing amount, with no period, and it is not the per-pay deduction; the samples do not fix its period (LTD 37.50 equals planDetail employeeContrib; LIFESAL equals employeePremium for one employee, 10.80, but not for another, 15.00 vs 9.00, unexplained), so it stays raw and fills no typed field. planDetail amounts read as monthly on one weekly employee (each voucher line is a quarter of them), too thin to fill amount_period."
  ],
  "fields": [
    {"route": ["/benefits/v1/getBenefitPlans", "/benefits/v1/getEmployeePremium"], "field": "errorCode", "use": "excluded", "reason": "Response envelope; success is HTTP 200 with errorCode 0 (D-021)."},
    {"route": ["/benefits/v1/getBenefitPlans", "/benefits/v1/getEmployeePremium"], "field": "errorMessage", "use": "excluded", "reason": "Response envelope (D-021)."},
    {"route": ["/benefits/v1/getBenefitPlans", "/benefits/v1/getEmployeePremium"], "field": "extension.any", "use": "excluded", "reason": "Response envelope extension point; never filled in the samples."},

